{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Belshazzar</b>, in the sense of ḥamra — this was the counsel of the wine that he drank and became drunk." "<b>Shegaltei</b> — like <b>והשגל</b> (and the queen who sits beside him), and it is the lady prepared for the king's bed; likewise <b>תשגלנה</b>, and it is the act." "<b>And his concubines</b> — his concubines. And behold he did two evils: that they all drank from the sacred vessels, and that they praised the gods of gold, wood, and stone."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:20:01.389119044Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}